              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed this just a bit, to add more flavor. I sauteed the red bell pepper with the garlic (which I added more of) and some chopped onion in a little evoo/butter before adding the condensed soup, water, tomato juice (I used V-8), the spices and tomato. To make it creamy without too much fat, I added a quarter cup of fat free evaporated milk. This was a nice tomato soup, perfectly spiced. The only issue I had was that I would have liked more tomatoes and tomato flavor. Next time, I'll use either less water and more tomato juice and I'll add more diced tomatoes. NOTE: This makes more than four servings, unless you have really happy soup eaters. More like six healthy servings."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clevercook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We purchased some tomato basil soup in a box. After trying the first one my spouse wanted to throw them all out. They truly were disgusting! I used them as the base for this recipe. I didn't add chives or garlic, but the rest was added and it was fabulous!! Definitely a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-12T00:55:28.987Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Folk"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We love this soup!! This is a family favourite, and have made it as written here and at times we have modified it a bit too. Definitely roast the peppers",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-01T03:24:54.903Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naomi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't have any chives, and used garlic powder instead of fresh, as well as canned diced tomatoes. I counted the juice of the canned tomatoes as enough \"tomato juice.\" Yummy spices, nice with the red pepper.",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-24T17:16:23.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula Todora Paula T"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband and I love tomato soup, and this was a nice change from the usual that I make. We love a smooth texture, so I pureed the peppers and diced tomatoes before adding, and it was wonderful. I will make this one again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-11T05:50:31.313Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim's Cooking Now"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used milk instead of the water, as always do with condensed tomato soup. I also halved the spices, and still found the spices to over power the tomato flavor. If you like a spicy tomato soup, then maybe this is recipe is for you. For me, when I have tomato soup, I like to taste the tomato, and have it be the predominant flavor. We all ate it with our grilled mozzarella paninis, but it's probably not a recipe that I'd make again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-10T16:44:08.777Z"
          },
